    "title": "Data or disk destruction",
    "desc": "A program overwrote or destroyed a storage device or the root filesystem - dd writing to a raw block device, mkfs reformatting one, wipefs / blkdiscard erasing it, shred of a device, or rm -rf / --no-preserve-root. This is the destructive endgame of a wiper or ransomware (MITRE T1485): it is not deleting a file but obliterating the medium. agent_destructive_action catches an agent deleting repos and dropping databases (account-scoped); this is the host-wide view of raw device and root-filesystem destruction, whoever runs it.",
